 '[{"text":"Real, erect, and diminished","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Virtual, inverted, and magnified","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Real, inverted, and diminished","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Virtual, erect, and diminished","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'In a compound microscope, the eyepiece forms a virtual, inverted, and highly magnified final image of the intermediate real image produced by the objective lens.'),
('NEET UG', 'Physics', 'Optics and Wave Phenomena', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Total internal reflection can occur only when light travels:',
 '[{"text":"From a rarer medium to a denser medium","isCorrect":false},{"text":"From a denser medium to a rarer medium, beyond the critical angle","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Through a perfect vacuum only","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Along the normal to the surface","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Total internal reflection requires light to travel from an optically denser medium into a rarer medium, striking the interface at an angle greater than the critical angle.'),

